"{\u0022id\u0022:210173,\u0022partnerCode\u0022:\u0022masc\u0022,\u0022documentCode\u0022:\u0022BBBA\u0022,\u0022collectionCode\u0022:\u0022bluehills\u0022,\u0022previousCode\u0022:null,\u0022title\u0022:\u0022File: BBBA - DISTRICT SCHOOL COMMITTEE MEMBER QUALIFICATIONS\u0022,\u0022status\u0022:1,\u0022version\u0022:1,\u0022parentDocId\u0022:210168,\u0022parentDocCode\u0022:null,\u0022parentDocTitle\u0022:null,\u0022masterDocId\u0022:204298,\u0022hasChildren\u0022:false,\u0022treeDepth\u0022:3,\u0022fileName\u0022:\u0022sop0000210173.html\u0022,\u0022anchor\u0022:null,\u0022isEmptyDoc\u0022:false,\u0022isPartialDoc\u0022:false,\u0022isViewable\u0022:true,\u0022showInToc\u0022:true,\u0022allowDownload\u0022:true,\u0022showWatermark\u0022:false,\u0022dtStart\u0022:\u00222001-01-01T00:00:00\u0022,\u0022dtEnd\u0022:\u00222900-12-31T00:00:00\u0022,\u0022dtAdopted\u0022:null,\u0022dtCreated\u0022:\u00222025-12-02T23:34:15.43\u0022,\u0022dtModified\u0022:\u00222025-12-02T23:34:15.43\u0022,\u0022dtFirstAdopted\u0022:null,\u0022dtReviewed\u0022:null,\u0022dtFirstReviewed\u0022:null,\u0022html\u0022:\u0022\u003C!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC \\\u0022-//W3C//DTD W3 HTML//EN\\\u0022\u003E\u003CHTML\u003E\u003CHEAD\u003E\\t\u003CLINK rel=\\\u0022stylesheet\\\u0022 href=\\\u0022/sopapi/document/getdocumentcollectioncss/masc/bluehillsset/bluehills\\\u0022 type=\\\u0022text/css\\\u0022\u003E\u003C/HEAD\u003E\u003CBODY \u003E\u003Ca id=\\\u0022sop0000031\\\u0022 name=\\\u0022sop0000031\\\u0022\u003E\u003C/a\u003E\u003Ca id=\\\u0022z2Code_BBBA\\\u0022 name=\\\u0022z2Code_BBBA\\\u0022\u003E\u003C/a\u003E\u003CH1 CLASS=\u0027Heading3\u0027\u003E\u003Cspan class-\u0027Underline\u0027\u003EFile\u003C/span\u003E: BBBA - DISTRICT SCHOOL COMMITTEE MEMBER QUALIFICATIONS\u003C/H1\u003E\u003CP CLASS=\u0027BodyText\u0027\u003EIn order to serve on the District School Committee, an individual must be a resident of one of the District\u0026acute;s member towns and a registered voter from the town in which he resides and must take an oath of office as required by law.\u003C/P\u003E\u003CP CLASS=\u0027BodyText\u0027\u003EAny person who is a resident of a member town and is a registered voter in the town in which he resides shall be entitled to have his name printed on the ballot to be used in the district-wide election if he shall file with the district clerk nomination papers signed by the number of voters as provided in section six who are registered and qualified to vote in the regional school district in which he resides.\u003C/P\u003E\u003CP CLASS=\u0027BodyText\u0027\u003ECommittee members shall be elected by way of district-wide, at large elections, with a residency requirements which will result in one resident of each member town having a position on the Committee.\u0026nbsp; That is, the candidate who receives the highest number of district-wide, at-large votes when compared to all other candidates who reside in the same member town shall be seated on the Committee.\u003C/P\u003E\u003CP CLASS=\u0027BodyText\u0027\u003EEach new member will present to the District Committee secretary official certification of having sworn the oath before an officer duly qualified to administer oaths prior to entering on his official duties as a member of the Committee.\u0026nbsp; From the Town Clerk, newly qualified Committee members, by law, receive, and sign a receipt for, a copy of the Massachusetts open meeting law governing the conduct of Committee meetings in general and executive sessions in particular.\u003C/P\u003E\u003CP CLASS=\u0027BodyText\u0027\u003EMembership on the District School Committee is not limited race, color, age, gender, sexual orientation, disability, religious or political conviction. \u003C/P\u003E\u003CP CLASS=\u0027BodyText\u0027\u003EThe District School Committee shall serve without compensation, except that\u0026nbsp; compensation may be authorized by majority vote of the voting member towns as authorized at their respective town meetings.\u003C/P\u003E\u003CP CLASS=\u0027BodyText\u0027\u003ENo member of the District School Committee shall be eligible to be employed in the position of teacher, administrator or superintendent of the District.\u003C/P\u003E\u003CP CLASS=\u0027LegalRefs\u0027\u003ELEGAL REFS.:\u0026nbsp; Chapter 10 of the Acts of 1988 \u003C/P\u003E\u003CP CLASS=\u0027LegalRefs-Indent\u0027\u003EM.G.L. \u003Ca  href=\u0027https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleIII/Chapter30A/section20\u0027 TARGET=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003E30A:20\u003C/A\u003E; \u003Ca  href=\u0027https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleVII/Chapter41/section107\u0027 TARGET=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003E41:107\u003C/A\u003E; \u003Ca  href=\u0027https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleVII/Chapter41/section109\u0027 TARGET=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003E41:109\u003C/A\u003E; \u003Ca  href=\u0027https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXII/Chapter71/section52\u0027 TARGET=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003E71:52\u003C/A\u003E; \u003Ca  href=\u0027https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXII/Chapter76/section5\u0027 TARGET=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003E76:5\u003C/A\u003E\u003C/P\u003E\u003C/BODY\u003E\u003C/HTML\u003E\u0022,\u0022versionNote\u0022:null}"